ORenIshii,ascended {73782}

O-Ren's maiden days in the dungeon ended as a lowly rothe killed her
beloved dog Hachi. Hachiko had been a very protective, cooperative
dog, always stealing an item or two from shops, never messing up with
pick-axes. She buried him and went on, for his dead not to be in vain.

What followed was a long list of unintended but unavoidable murders.
First she angered the priest in Minetown and had to kill all the
Guards.  The Watch Captain's saber nearly ended her quest but the
second of those unidentified wands she took from the cold hands of a
previous adventurer put that guy to sleep, never to rise again. Said
priest followed shortly afterward, for O-Ren Ishii was quick with the
yumi and ya.

As she found some blessed scrolls of Identify, she thought she'd go
back to that largish scroll shop to try her luck. Sadly, as she wanted
to buy some of the scrolls the shop keeper decided that he's going to
charge her for all she holds (finger slipped). Or so were his last
words.

Later on, back in Minetown, a black sphere would disrupt O-Ren's mind
and she'd bump into a shop keeper who'd have done better to forget
about the accident.

She tried to calm down a little in the main dungeon and did what all
female Samurai do when they are depressed. She went to a general
store.  Something on the way managed to blind her and you can imagine
that there weren't a lot of floating eyes wandering around by now...
Needless to say, O-Ren bumped into the shop owner and that spoiled the
otherwise cozy shop atmosphere.

All in all apart from that other shop, it can be said to her defense
that she left an armor shop up there on level 3 or so.

The bag problem went along quite deep into the game and she formed
complicated stash networks, sometimes carrying chests or large boxes
to protect her scrolls and sake. The latter was possible because she
was quite tough and could lay hands on a gray dragon and his scales
shortly after Sokoban.

On the other hand there was only one magic marker, ?oEA and EW were
not found in abundance during the whole game, and priests tended not
to have robes until late.

Well, Ashikaga Takauji fell to a death ray as did the Wizard (8 times)
and then came the planes and that was it, basically. She brought a
white dragon into Heaven for Hachi to have a pet all for himself.


